<<
/Alt (Two forest plots depict odds ratios for studies based on ethnicity. In plot \(A\), studies are categorized into "Caucasian" and "Asian" subgroups, with overall odds ratio 1.17 \(95% CI: 1.06, 1.29, p=0.002\). In plot \(B\), similar subgroups are shown, with an overall odds ratio of 1.13 \(95% CI: 0.96, 1.33, p=0.228\). Each study displays odds ratio, confidence interval, and weight. A diamond indicates subgroup summaries, and heterogeneity statistics are included below each plot.)
